Package: spilloverID
Type: Package
Title: Reservoir Identification for Zoonotic Spillover Without Genetic Data
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-09-09
Authors@R: c(
    person("Benjamin", "Roche", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "benjamin.roche@ird.fr",
           comment = "IRD, UMI 209 UMMISCO"))
Description: Implements a composite epidemiological plausibility score (Pi)
    to identify the most likely wildlife reservoir of a zoonotic pathogen
    when only serological and exposure data are available (no genetic data).
    The score combines 14 independent epidemiological signatures spanning
    spatial, individual, multi-level, demographic, temporal, mechanistic and
    specificity dimensions, together with three maintenance signatures
    (C12-C14) that separate a maintenance reservoir from an amplifying or
    bridge host. The package also provides a mechanistic simulation engine
    to validate inference under known ground truth.
    See Roche et al. (2026) for the methodological framework, and
    Viana et al. (2014) <doi:10.1016/j.tree.2014.03.002> for the underlying
    "assembling evidence" approach.
